What are Parameters -

    Let's start with the A Basic computer programming
    Input => Output

    Estimate Rent Program:
    1.  Multiply the sq.ft by 5
    2.  Multiply the floor number by 20
    3.  Add them

    These are the methods how to calculate the rent according to an expert
    We write program to take input of sq.ft and floor number => we will get rent as output

    |

    Along the way machine learning came.
    Machine learning?
        This is not by explicitly programming to do the tasks but rather learning from the data on how to do it.
    So the computer program is replaced by a model based on hypothesis.

    For example:

        Let's understand a simple hypothesis, the rest hypothesis i.e In our case the rent depends only
        on (No.of square feet) and (what floor it's on). Then our model might be like "Okay" let's take a quantity "A"
        and multiply with (square feet) and let's take a quantity "B" and multiple with (floor number) and add them to
        give us the rent, where "A" and "B" are still to be set. How do we set that "A" and "B"? Let's look at the data.

        There are 2 phases in which we work with Machine Learning.

        1. Training:
            i)   When you look at a lots of examples in this case lots of examples of apartments. a) How much it costs to
            rent them, b) How much for a sq ft, and c)  Which floor they are in.
            ii)  In our case all of these examples will help use to figure out how can we set "A" and "B" in the best
            possible way.
            iii) Once we predict "A" and "B" then we move to (Inference learning).
            iv)  That "A" and "B" are set now. We are not gonna touch those 2 values. Now we are going to predict new
            apartment's rent which is not used while training the model this is something new. If we have done a good
            job the values will be accurate
        2. Inference learning - This has already been explained in previous modules

    & That "A" and "B" are what we call as Parameters or weights, but in real world that apartment rent can depend on
    other parameters i.e "C", "D" and "E" and so on...., and a typical ML model might have anywhere from
    20-200 parameters controlling how it makes it's predictions.

    To conclude -
    Parameters are nothing but a piece of information that it fixed/set to model while training it.
    ML models are like 20-200, but the gpt-4 is more that billions parameters.
    So just imagine how much scale we are currently in that's huge.


